cff-version: 1.2.0
message: |
  SpektraLab is a native macOS application and C++ Metal render engine built on
  Andrea Volpato's `spektrafilm`, which is where the film simulation, the
  measured profiles and the print+scan model come from.

  **If you are citing the science, cite spektrafilm, not this.** The physical
  modelling, the profile measurements and the RA-4 print simulation are that
  project's contribution; see the `references` section below and
  https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm. Cite this repository only when
  you mean the application, the C++ port of the engine, or the GPU pipeline.

  SpektraLab is GPL-3.0-or-later; the profiles and the LUTs baked from them are
  CC BY-SA 4.0 and remain Andrea Volpato's work. SpektraLab is not affiliated
  with or endorsed by the spektrafilm project.

title: "SpektraLab: a macOS application for spectral film and print simulation"
abstract: |
  SpektraLab develops a scene-linear photograph through a virtual film
  negative and a print, on the GPU, interactively. It is a SwiftUI application
  with a C++/Metal port of the spektrafilm render engine compiled into it, held
  to the Python reference at float32 storage epsilon by a set of parity
  harnesses. It contributes the application and the engine port; the spectral
  modelling it renders is spektrafilm's.

authors:
